ui/editor/langs — third-party data notice
==========================================

The files under data/ and testdata/tokenize/ are generated by gen/export.mjs
and contain data converted from Monaco Editor:

  - data/<id>.json         Monarch grammars, language configurations and
                           language registrations from the npm package
                           monaco-editor@0.56.0
                           (esm/vs/languages/definitions/*).
                           data/vue.json reuses the html grammar and
                           configuration under a separate "vue" id.
  - data/themes.json       The base themes vs, vs-dark, hc-black, hc-light
                           from monaco-editor@0.56.0
                           (esm/vs/editor/standalone/common/themes.js).
  - testdata/tokenize/*    Tokenization test cases from
                           https://github.com/microsoft/monaco-editor
                           tag v0.56.0, src/languages/definitions/**/*.test.ts.

The exporter converts the data to JSON and makes these changes; the grammar,
configuration, theme and test values themselves are not edited:

  - Regular expressions are written as {"$regex": source, "flags": flags}.
    Object properties whose value is undefined are dropped and undefined
    array elements become null (JSON has no undefined).
  - Each data/<id>.json wraps one registration as {registrationOrder,
    registration, language, conf}. "registrationOrder" is added: the
    position in Monaco's registration sequence (register.all.js order, then
    vue). "registration" is normalized: only id, extensions, filenames,
    filenamePatterns, aliases, mimetypes and firstLine are kept (the loader
    function is dropped), and missing fields are filled with defaults
    ([] for lists, "" for firstLine).
  - data/vue.json is not a Monaco registration: it is added to match
    MinCode's .vue registration (id "vue", extension .vue, aliases Vue/vue,
    MIME text/x-vue) and carries copies of the html grammar and
    configuration.
  - data/themes.json keeps only the base, inherit, rules and colors fields
    of each base theme.
  - testdata/tokenize/<id>.json merges the cases of every test file that
    targets the same main language id (pgsql.test.ts and redshift.test.ts
    test "sql", so their cases are in sql.json), in file order, keeping only
    the first copy of byte-identical cases.

